        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span>
          <span>1. Mathematical Derivation: From Constant Product to Bounded Virtual Reserves</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          In a classical Uniswap v2 constant-product automated market maker, the invariant is defined across infinite price space <code class="font-mono text-emerald-400">x &middot; y = k</code>. Let <code class="font-mono text-slate-200">P_0</code> denote the entry price of token X in terms of token Y, and let price change by ratio <code class="font-mono text-slate-200">k = P_1 / P_0</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The classic impermanent loss formula represents the percentage change in the liquidity provider's portfolio value relative to simply holding the original tokens:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/90 border border-slate-800 p-5 rounded-xl font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-cyan-300 my-4">
          IL_v2(k) = (V_LP - V_hold) / V_hold = (2 &middot; &radic;k) / (1 + k) - 1
        </div>

        <p>
          In Uniswap v3, liquidity is bounded within discrete price boundaries <code class="font-mono text-emerald-400">[p_a, p_b]</code>. Real tokens are offset by <em>virtual reserves</em> <code class="font-mono text-slate-200">x_v = L / &radic;p_b</code> and <code class="font-mono text-slate-200">y_v = L &middot; &radic;p_a</code>, satisfying:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/90 border border-slate-800 p-5 rounded-xl font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-emerald-400 my-4">
          (x + L / &radic;p_b) &middot; (y + L &middot; &radic;p_a) = L&sup2;
        </div>

        <p>
          The real reserves held by a position with liquidity <code class="font-mono text-slate-200">L</code> at current price <code class="font-mono text-slate-200">P &isin; [p_a, p_b]</code> are explicitly given by:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-4 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
            <span class="text-cyan-400 block font-bold mb-1">Real Token X Reserves:</span>
            x(P) = L &middot; (1 / &radic;P - 1 / &radic;p_b)
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
            <span class="text-emerald-400 block font-bold mb-1">Real Token Y Reserves:</span>
            y(P) = L &middot; (&radic;P - &radic;p_a)
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>
          Evaluating the portfolio value in numeraire <code class="font-mono text-slate-200">Y</code>: <code class="font-mono text-slate-200">V_v3(P) = x(P) &middot; P + y(P)</code> yields:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/90 border border-slate-800 p-5 rounded-xl font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-cyan-300 my-4">
          V_v3(P) = L &middot; [2 &middot; &radic;P - P / &radic;p_b - &radic;p_a]
        </div>

        <p>
          Comparing this to the initial deposit holding value <code class="font-mono text-slate-200">V_hold(P_1) = x_0 &middot; P_1 + y_0</code> yields the exact concentrated impermanent loss equation:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-slate-950 border border-emerald-500/40 p-5 rounded-xl font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-emerald-300 my-4">
          IL_v3(P_1) = [ V_v3(P_1) - V_hold(P_1) ] / V_hold(P_1)
          <br/><br/>
          Inside Range: IL_v3 = - L &middot; &radic;P_0 &middot; (&radic;k - 1)&sup2; / [ P_1 &middot; (1/&radic;P_0 - 1/&radic;p_b) + (&radic;P_0 - &radic;p_a) ]
        </div>

        <p>
          Notice that while the numerator matches the absolute dollar divergence of Uniswap v2, the denominator is reduced by the capital efficiency factor <code class="font-mono text-amber-400">&eta; &asymp; 1 / (1 - &radic;(p_a / p_b))</code>. Thus, <strong>narrowing your liquidity interval magnifies your impermanent loss percentage by exactly the same leverage factor that magnifies your fee yield</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>

